# Testing & validation

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `docs/DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md` for the full delivery protocol.

## Rust

- Domain gates: `cargo test -p talaria-quality`
- Source connector fixtures: `cargo test -p talaria-sources`
- Targeted API/store tests: `cargo test -p talaria-api <module>` or `cargo test -p talaria-store <module>`
- Build: `cargo check -p <changed-crate>`
- Lint: `cargo clippy -p <changed-crate> --all-targets`
- Database-backed tests require PostgreSQL with PostGIS, matching the CI job.

## Frontend

- `cd web && npm test` (Vitest)
- `cd web && npm run build` (includes TypeScript typechecking)
- For user-facing changes, also validate actual browser behavior on desktop and mobile. Unit tests do not replace visual checks.

## Reporting

Report exact commands, results, environment limitations and any tests **not run**. Never say "tests passed" when they were not executed. Separate existing warnings from new failures.
